p.src:
For the constant function, $\begin{aligned}
 \{1^2,p\}
 &=1\{1,p\}+\{1,p\}1
 =2\{1,p\}.\end{aligned}$ Since $1^2=1$, this says $\{1,p\}=2\{1,p\}$, hence $\{1,p\}=0$. Next, $\{q,p\}=1.$ For the next monomial, $\{q^2,p\}
 =q\{q,p\}+\{q,p\}q
 =2q.$

