p.src:
Self-brackets vanish by antisymmetry, so only the mixed bracket needs work: $\begin{aligned}
 \{Q,P\}
 &=\{-\sin\theta\,p+\cos\theta\,q,\,
       \cos\theta\,p+\sin\theta\,q\}\notag\\
 &=\cos^2\theta\,\{q,p\}
   -\sin^2\theta\,\{p,q\}\notag\\
 &=\cos^2\theta+\sin^2\theta=1.
 \end{aligned}$

