p.src:
Write one small step as $Q=q+\delta q,\qquad P=p+\delta p,$ where $\delta q$ and $\delta p$ are themselves functions of phase space. Infinitesimal means that terms quadratic and higher in these changes may be discarded. Expanding the transformed bracket gives $\begin{aligned}
 \{Q,P\}
 &=\{q+\delta q,p+\delta p\}\notag\\
 &=\{q,p\}+\{\delta q,p\}+\{q,\delta p\}
   +\{\delta q,\delta p\}.
 \end{aligned}$ The last term is second order. Therefore the first-order canonical condition is $\{\delta q,p\}=-\{q,\delta p\}.$

