p.src:
The same generator controls every function. By the chain rule, $\begin{aligned}
 \delta A
 &=\frac{\partial A}{\partial q}\delta q
   +\frac{\partial A}{\partial p}\delta p\notag\\
 &=\epsilon\left(
 \frac{\partial A}{\partial q}\frac{\partial G}{\partial p}
 -\frac{\partial A}{\partial p}\frac{\partial G}{\partial q}
 \right)\notag\\
 &=\epsilon\{A,G\}.
 \end{aligned}$ For many degrees of freedom the sum over $i$ is understood, and each $\delta q_i$ may depend on every $q_j$ and $p_j$, not only on the pair with the same index.

