p.src:
Only canonical pairs contribute: $\{x,p_x\}=1,\qquad \{y,p_y\}=1,$ while $\{x,p_y\}=\{y,p_x\}=0$. Expanding, $\begin{aligned}
 \{G,H\}
 &=\frac{1}{2m}
 \{xp_y-yp_x,p_x^2+p_y^2\}\notag\\
 &=\frac{1}{2m}\{xp_y,p_x^2\}
  +\frac{1}{2m}\{xp_y,p_y^2\}\notag\\
 &\quad-\frac{1}{2m}\{yp_x,p_x^2\}
  -\frac{1}{2m}\{yp_x,p_y^2\}.\end{aligned}$ The two cross-mismatched terms vanish. The remaining terms are $\begin{aligned}
 \{xp_y,p_x^2\}
 &=p_y\{x,p_x^2\}=2p_xp_y,\notag\\
 \{yp_x,p_y^2\}
 &=p_x\{y,p_y^2\}=2p_xp_y.\end{aligned}$ They cancel: $\{G,H\}
 =\frac{1}{2m}\left(2p_xp_y-2p_xp_y\right)=0.$

